should you focus on speed or perfection  i got a great question from one of my  youtube viewers pac media who wrote in  long comment basically saying developed  an idea with a professor  could have a huge impact professor  saying wait make it perfect plan it all  out before you launch  and pack media wants to get started make  it fast get it out there right now  entrepreneur mindset and what do i do  what should i do as a question so here's  the thing  you want to embrace a genius at the end  and do both  and the best way to marry that concept  is what's called a minimum viable  product  so this is a product that is good enough  to get out there  it's not some crappy thing you've thrown  together that nobody's interested in  because you have to go speed  is good enough to make a difference but  it's not fully out researched everything  planned out  if you talk to academia  and not to slam on academia  but they're very research driven  right they want everything done if you  look at what they have to do in their  daily lives and create papers and  journals everything has to be cited  everything has to be perfect if you  don't have a great paper with everything  cited you're not going to get published  so that's the mindset they're coming  from  but there aren't too many  academia who are great entrepreneurs  so keep that in mind where you're  getting your advice from  i know you want to get out there  and that's one of the best ways to start  getting feedback is start talking to  your customers build it around their  problems so think about what your  minimum viable product is what does that  look like you have a huge feature list  and and we all have this in our business  we all have a to-do list this big of  things we want to add in things we want  to make better  think about the what needs to be in this  product for people to start picking it  up and finding value in it  that's what you launch with  and launch as fast as you can with that  product and get feedback because no  matter how well you think you're  planning it out you're never gonna do a  great job  i was a victim of this in my business my  first software company we had a great  product okay it was super easy to use is  biotech software helping find cures  in research for cancer and aids and  diabetes and doing great work  the thing that i  spent a ton of time on  and the thing that my development team  spent a ton of time on we thought was  really helpful really valuable super  useful  turns out  that  our audience didn't really care about it  they cared a little bit but it wasn't  great  and my researchers the people on my team  they were in the field right they knew  this stuff it's not like we're just  designing for some customer base that we  don't know about they were the customers  and they built it around something they  felt was a need but we didn't test it  with the market and we ended up spending  a ton of time on this feature that  nobody really cared about where it could  have been better spent on something else  so if i had to make my great plan from  the beginning what i think the product  should look like that would have been it  and a bunch of other stuff would have  been in  and we would have made a mistake  because you can only really judge when  you start talking to your customers and  get their feedback and see if they're  willing to buy it or not  you can have the greatest plan in the  world but if nobody pays you then it's a  sucky plan  and you don't know until you get out  there so don't spend two years making  this great plan only to find out that it  doesn't work  on the flip side you need something to  go and show people  so start talking to them  get out there make your minimum viable  product figure out what features you  need to have in that product  for people to be willing to try it out  and then take their feedback see what  they say and make your product better  and what they suggest may be completely  different than the roadmap you set up  for yourself and that's okay because  you're building it around people who are  going to pay you and that's going to be  your lifeline and help you build a great  company i know it's a struggle i know as  entrepreneurs we want things out quickly  but you got to balance speed versus  perfection  it's a question that'll keep coming back  over and over and over again and the  best way to solve it is building around  your customers  believe and good luck  for those of you watching like the video  thumbs up below thank you guys and i  want to hear you have to think please  leave a comment below i love seeing them  they make my day every day really i love  the comments even if you've never left a  comment today's your day leave a comment  please just saying you love the video or  whatever you have to think and you have  a question for your business leave it  below i'll make a video response thank  you guys i'll see you soon
 

